# MadGraph5 batch script: e+ e- > mu+ mu- NP<=1
# in SMEFTsim_topU3l_MwScheme (UFO v3.0.2), restricted by restrict_vg_c4l.dat.
#
# Why this exact process:
#   Scalar and vector four-fermion contact operators across two lepton flavours.
#   This is the row where one UFO vertex carries both spinor pairings -- (1,2)(3,4)
#   and (1,4)(2,3) -- so MadGraph's per-structure permutation sign
#   (`import_ufo.get_sign_flow`) is observable rather than conventional.
#
# The model path is repo-relative to the vendored UFO; build.sh rewrites it to
# the work-area copy it stages under output/models/, which is where the
# vg_* restrict cards of validation/madgraph/cards/smeft/ are placed. Both
# generators therefore prune vertices from the same card.
#
# `display interactions` prints the count MadGraph's own interaction splitting
# arrives at (one interaction per coupling-order tuple, import_ufo.add_interaction)
# into the build log, which is where extract_interactions.py reads it from.
#
# Orders are explicit because SMEFTsim gives NP hierarchy 99: MadGraph's default
# WEIGHTED bound would drop every diagram carrying a Wilson coefficient.
import model validation/ufo/SMEFTsim_topU3l_MwScheme_UFO-vg_c4l
display interactions
generate e+ e- > mu+ mu- NP<=1
output ee_to_mumu_4f -nojpeg
launch
set lpp1 0
set lpp2 0
set ebeam1 250
set ebeam2 250
set use_syst False
done
